Hesperid 3 is a refining works on the [[Phenomena/Joker World|Joker world]] the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]] stands on, a hundred miles east of the misted crater. It is one low building, half sunk into the ground, raised from steel cut off some larger craft the builders had wrecked. Red lamps line its outside. Its front door is a tall pair of interlocking teeth; a round fisheye aperture on the right side lets a monorail track pass in and out, and the track runs north from the building and along its halls. The walls are cased in an alloy of iron, carbon and boron that no smith in [[Færrin]] can make, and much of the interior, down to the linings of its barrels, is pure titanium. The inside stays lit, cool and dry; its machines still pull the water out of the air.

The works were built by a company from beyond the firmament whose mark is a triangle of sixteen dots, fifteen small ones turned about a sixteenth at the centre. The company's people had been shipwrecked in the Far Realms long before, and raised Hesperid 3 to refine [[Phenomena/Phlogiston|phlogiston]], shipping the fuel north by rail to the [[Geography/Hesperid|Hesperid]], their ship and the base they called HQ. A console by the front door kept their mail and their lights. A second console in the back rooms charts the company's rail: a line north from Hesperid 3 to the Hesperid, and from the Hesperid out to Hesperid 1 and Hesperid 2. The line from HQ to those two is struck through as broken, and the line up from Hesperid 3 is drawn as six lines packed so close they read as one, with HQ itself showing six barely offset afterimages.

Three were left to run it: Sergeant [[People/Ulrich Benda|Ulrich Benda]], Sybil and Thurston. Their logs run from the year 72 to 121. HQ stopped answering; Sybil died on her cot, old age by Ulrich's guess, though she had once ridden the train north toward HQ and come back empty-handed; Thurston fell into a pool and came away burned all over. Ulrich's last entry says the two of them abandoned HQ's protocol to work faster, and that they left. The three of them walk the works still, dead and risen as [[Bestiary/Undead|once was]].

The works hold the fruit of all that work: barrels of the red fuel, four of them racked in a modified locomotive walled with magic of space and time and luck that was never finished, its windows dark. A pool of red liquid bubbles under the pipes beside the console, and the console reports the refinement cell breached. Where the works draw off their fuel, one intake spigot has been duplicated five times over, six spigots joined to a single tube and five of them hooked to nothing, smooth enough that the shape could have been made that way. Nothing about it reads as a curse, and the same six-fold pattern shows on the Hesperid.

The back rooms of the works are given over to [[Bestiary/Undead|things from beyond]], figures of red flame that wander them.
